WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.640
Prompt injection defenses should be tested before and after deployment.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:12.980
Testing should be safe, scoped, and defensive, with the goal of validating trust boundaries, controls, approvals, monitoring, and data exposure assumptions.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:27.520
Testing may include reviewing how the model handles untrusted documents, verifying tool permissions, checking approval workflows, confirming that sensitive data is not exposed unnecessarily, and ensuring output validation blocks unsafe downstream use.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:36.220
Teams should also monitor production behavior, review incidents and near misses, update threat models, and improve controls as new patterns emerge.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:43.480
Prompt injection risk changes as prompts, models, tools, retrieval sources, data, and user workflows change.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.660
Prompt injection is not a one-time checklist item.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:54.960
It is an ongoing AI application security concern that requires design, testing, monitoring, response, and continuous improvement.
